	(617, "CVE-1999-1265", "1998-09-22T04:00:00.000", "2025-04-03T01:03:51.193", "SMTP server in SLmail 3.1 and earlier allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service via malformed commands whose arguments begin with a \"(\" (parenthesis) character, such as (1) SEND, (2) VRFY, (3) EXPN, (4) MAIL FROM, (5) RCPT TO."),
