	(619, "CVE-1999-1228", "1998-09-27T04:00:00.000", "2025-04-03T01:03:51.193", "Various modems that do not implement a guard time, or are configured with a guard time of 0, can allow remote attackers to execute arbitrary modem commands such as ATH, ATH0, etc., via a \"+++\" sequence that appears in ICMP packets, the subject of an e-mail message, IRC commands, and others."),
